Applies on top of tools/kmc-as-hilo-libultra.patch (independent of it: also applies straight after
tools/kmc-as-libultra-nops.patch). Game units only.

`li.s $fN,c` with c != 0 becomes a load from a pool entry the assembler adds to .rodata:
    lui $at,%hi(pool); lwc1 $fN,%lo(pool)($at)
instead of stock gas's -G0 form `lui $at,c>>16; [ori $at,$at,c&0xffff;] mtc1 $at,$fN`. On by default when
--no-float-doubleword is given (all 23 game units, none of the library units); `--pool-float-literals` /
`--no-pool-float-literals` force it either way, so no Makefile change is needed.

ROM evidence (expected/ objects of the 23 game units, pool values read from baserom.z64):
  - 0 sites of `lui $at,imm; mtc1 $at,$fN` (or lui/ori/mtc1). Every mtc1 in the game code moves $zero (539) or an
    integer that is then converted (cvt.s.w), or a float GCC itself kept in an integer register
    (func_801A6170 `lui s1,0x40e0 ... mtc1 s1,$f4`; func_801A44F8/func_801AEE04 `lui v0,0x8000` are sign-bit masks).
  - 3751 single `lui $at; lwc1 $fN,%lo(D_8010xxxx)($at)` loads from the game rodata, 2702 of them of a value whose
    low 16 bits are zero (which stock gas would have built with lui/mtc1): 1.0f 420 loads from 391 different
    addresses, 2.0f 175/151, 10.0f 115/99 ... one pool entry per use, never shared: an assembler pool, not GCC's.
  - The library objects do have the immediate form (45 lui/mtc1 + 3 lui/ori/mtc1) and keep it: they do not pass
    --no-float-doubleword.
0.0 never reaches the assembler as li.s (GCC writes `mtc1 $0,$fN`, and `mtc1 $0,$fN; mtc1 $0,$fN+1` for a double);
a hand-written `li.s $fN,0` keeps the immediate form. `li.s $rN,c` into an integer register (float arguments in
$a1-$a3, 285 uses in the current game units) is untouched.

Section: .rodata (the section stock gas already uses for `li.d` at -G0), aligned to 4, one entry per li.s in source
order, no merging. .lit4 would need $gp (`lwc1 $fN,%gp_rel(pool)($gp)`, one instruction) and is what -G0 rules out;
.rodata through $at gives the ROM's two instructions.

Verified 2026-11-20 with the as_verify method: no function lost, no library object changed, 21 of 23 game objects
byte-identical; the two that change hold unmatched drafts that use float literals (func_80120D18 99.44 -> 99.49,
func_80112F80 99.07 -> 99.80).

Re-apply with: git apply --ignore-whitespace tools/kmc-as-pool-float.patch

